#: ../../source/chapters/09-lazy-scrum-team.md:56
#: 7eceb0632ae64873af87f7b9fdb06e33
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Scrum {cite}`schwaber2020scrum` supplies the role vocabulary; the skill's "
"innovation is less about roles and more about what happens *between* them. "
"Conway's Law {cite}`conway1968law` reminds us that the communication "
"structure leaks into the artefact structure; the skill uses this as a "
"feature rather than a bug — the hand-off artefacts *are* the communication "
"channel."
msgstr ""
"Scrum {cite}`schwaber2020scrum` 提供了这份角色词汇表；这个技能的创新并不在于角色本身，而在于角色 *之间* "
"发生了什么。Conway 律 {cite}`conway1968law` "
"提醒我们：沟通结构会渗进制品结构；这个技能把这件事当作特性而不是缺陷——那些交接制品 *本身* 就是沟通通道。"

#: ../../source/chapters/09-lazy-scrum-team.md:63
#: 1d89ca3b511d4f64851b1397678f6f41
msgid "§09.2 — Pattern 1 — Artefact State Model"
msgstr "§09.2 —— 模式一 —— 制品状态机"

#: ../../source/chapters/09-lazy-scrum-team.md:65
#: 6dfad2ef7e954cdf96c04b29b4a43c7c
msgid ""
"Every reviewable artefact in the harness has exactly four states — `draft → "
"review → approved → archived` — with tightly constrained transitions. The "
"canonical encoding ships as a YAML file any ticketing system can import:"
msgstr ""
"挽具中每一份可评审制品都恰好有四种状态——`draft → review → approved → archived`——且跃迁被严格约束。权威编码以 "
"YAML 文件交付，任何 ticket 系统都能导入："

#: ../../source/chapters/09-lazy-scrum-team.md:70
#: 693e519453ad4b858826e5c73d9f94a0
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"# verified: 2026-04-17 · Ch.09 lazy-scrum-team hands-on · adaptable state machine\n"
"artefact_state_model_version: \"0.1\"\n"
"states:\n"
"  draft:     {color: \"#bbb\"}\n"
"  review:    {color: \"#f4c\"}\n"
"  approved:  {color: \"#4c8\"}\n"
"  archived:  {color: \"#888\"}\n"
"transitions:\n"
"  - {from: draft,    to: review,   by: Author,           trigger: submit}\n"
"  - {from: review,   to: draft,    by: Reviewer,         trigger: request_changes}\n"
"  - {from: review,   to: approved, by: FinalAcceptance,  trigger: approve}\n"
"  - {from: approved, to: archived, by: ReleaseManager,   trigger: release_shipped}\n"
"  - {from: archived, to: review,   by: Author,           trigger: reopen}\n"
"invariants:\n"
"  - only_FinalAcceptance_can_approve\n"
"  - no_skip_review_from_draft_to_approved\n"
"  - archived_artefacts_are_read_only_until_reopened\n"
msgstr ""
"# verified: 2026-04-17 · Ch.09 lazy-scrum-team hands-on · adaptable state machine\n"
"artefact_state_model_version: \"0.1\"\n"
"states:\n"
"  draft:     {color: \"#bbb\"}\n"
"  review:    {color: \"#f4c\"}\n"
"  approved:  {color: \"#4c8\"}\n"
"  archived:  {color: \"#888\"}\n"
"transitions:\n"
"  - {from: draft,    to: review,   by: Author,           trigger: submit}\n"
"  - {from: review,   to: draft,    by: Reviewer,         trigger: request_changes}\n"
"  - {from: review,   to: approved, by: FinalAcceptance,  trigger: approve}\n"
"  - {from: approved, to: archived, by: ReleaseManager,   trigger: release_shipped}\n"
"  - {from: archived, to: review,   by: Author,           trigger: reopen}\n"
"invariants:\n"
"  - only_FinalAcceptance_can_approve\n"
"  - no_skip_review_from_draft_to_approved\n"
"  - archived_artefacts_are_read_only_until_reopened\n"

#: ../../source/chapters/09-lazy-scrum-team.md:74
#: 22ac457f39084edf983c8025d9996072
msgid ""
"Two invariants make the state model load-bearing rather than decorative: "
"only Final Acceptance can flip `review → approved`, and approved artefacts "
"cannot return to `draft` without passing through `archived` first. These two"
" invariants together eliminate the most common failure mode of review "
"processes — silent rework — because any regression on an approved artefact "
"is visible as an explicit reopen event."
msgstr ""
"有两条不变量，让这个状态机成为承重的、而非装饰性的：只有 Final Acceptance 能翻转 `review → "
"approved`；已被批准的制品，要回到 `draft`，必须先经过 "
"`archived`。这两条不变量合在一起，消除了评审流程里最常见的那种失败模式——*沉默返工*——因为任何对\"已批准制品\"的回退，都会显式地表现为一次"
" reopen 事件。"

#: ../../source/chapters/09-lazy-scrum-team.md:82
#: 4f5e39805b354136ad08b3333580a72f
msgid "§09.3 — Pattern 2 — Rework Matrix"
msgstr "§09.3 —— 模式二 —— 返工矩阵"

#: ../../source/chapters/09-lazy-scrum-team.md:84
#: c9af13f5ea0f42e9892e1fee826956b4
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"The Rework Matrix names, for every finder × fixer pair, the specific "
"artefact that must accompany the hand-off. Pull-request-as-workflow research"
" {cite}`gousios2014pullbased` and the classic specification-by-example "
"corpus {cite}`adzic2011specbyexample` both argue for machine-readable hand-"
"offs; the Rework Matrix is this book's opinionated encoding."
msgstr ""
"返工矩阵针对每一对\"发现者 × 修复者\"，命名了必须随附这次交接的那件具体制品。把 PR 作为工作流的研究 "
"{cite}`gousios2014pullbased`，以及经典的 specification-by-example 文献 "
"{cite}`adzic2011specbyexample`，都主张\"机器可读的交接\"；返工矩阵是本书对此的一份带倾向的编码。"

#: ../../source/chapters/09-lazy-scrum-team.md:91
#: 4720044ee420413ead37d0011ea50ce5
msgid ""
"<!-- verified: 2026-04-17 · Ch.09 lazy-scrum-team hands-on · adaptable version -->\n"
"\n"
"# Rework Matrix (adaptable)\n"
"\n"
"Copy this file into your own repo under `docs/rework/README.md`. Adjust\n"
"the row/column set to your team's role cast; the *shape* — finder × fixer,\n"
"with a named rework artefact per cell — is what matters.\n"
"\n"
"|               | PO       | Architect | Developer | Test Engineer | Final Acceptance |\n"
"|---------------|----------|-----------|-----------|---------------|------------------|\n"
"| **PO**        | —        | `spec-delta.md`   | —                | `acceptance.md`        | —                          |\n"
"| **Architect** | —        | —                 | `adr-rework.md`  | —                      | —                          |\n"
"| **Developer** | `spec-question.md` | —       | —                | —                      | —                          |\n"
"| **Test**      | `acceptance-gap.md` | —      | `bug-report.md`  | —                      | —                          |\n"
"| **Final Acc** | `reject-reason.md` | `reject-reason.md` | `reject-reason.md` | `reject-reason.md` | —                     |\n"
"\n"
"Rule: no defect crosses a hand-off without a rework artefact attached.\n"
"\"Just fix it\" is an anti-pattern that burns institutional memory.\n"
msgstr ""
"<!-- verified: 2026-04-17 · Ch.09 lazy-scrum-team hands-on · adaptable version -->\n"
"\n"
"# 返工矩阵（可改写）\n"
"\n"
"把这份文件拷进你自己仓库的 `docs/rework/README.md`。把行列集合改成\n"
"你团队实际的角色班底；真正重要的是 *形状*——发现者 × 修复者，\n"
"每一格配一件署名返工制品。\n"
"\n"
"|               | PO       | Architect | Developer | Test Engineer | Final Acceptance |\n"
"|---------------|----------|-----------|-----------|---------------|------------------|\n"
"| **PO**        | —        | `spec-delta.md`   | —                | `acceptance.md`        | —                          |\n"
"| **Architect** | —        | —                 | `adr-rework.md`  | —                      | —                          |\n"
"| **Developer** | `spec-question.md` | —       | —                | —                      | —                          |\n"
"| **Test**      | `acceptance-gap.md` | —      | `bug-report.md`  | —                      | —                          |\n"
"| **Final Acc** | `reject-reason.md` | `reject-reason.md` | `reject-reason.md` | `reject-reason.md` | —                     |\n"
"\n"
"规则：任何缺陷跨过一次交接，都必须随附一份返工制品。\n"
"\"你就赶紧修一下吧\"是一种反模式，会烧掉组织记忆。\n"

#: ../../source/chapters/09-lazy-scrum-team.md:95
#: 2df920f85b064212ac4158b5de646550
msgid ""
"Concretely: when a Test Engineer rejects a Developer's PR, the rejection "
"lands as a `bug-report.md` file in the PR body, not as a Slack message. When"
" the PO rejects the Architect's ADR, it lands as a `spec-delta.md` under "
"`docs/rework/<sprint>/`. The named file is the contract; \"just fix it\" "
"comments are institutional amnesia."
msgstr ""
"具体地说：当 Test Engineer 驳回一位 Developer 的 PR，驳回意见以一份 `bug-report.md` 的形式落到 PR "
"body 里，而不是变成一条 Slack 消息。当 PO 驳回 Architect 的 ADR，驳回意见以一份 `spec-delta.md` "
"的形式落到 `docs/rework/<sprint>/` 下。*署名的那份文件* 就是契约；\"赶紧修一下\"式的评论，等于组织级失忆。"

